    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d319">

                <pb facs="0475" n="465" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg465"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/9–1845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hurley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-09-18T17:00:00+07:00">September 18,
                            1945—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 18—4:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1612. Favorable developments in Government-Communist negotiations indicated.
                    Slight delay in my departure might be helpful in situation.</p>
                <pb facs="0476" n="466" xml:id="pg466"/>
                <p>Accordingly General Wedemeyer is proceeding to Washington, leaving Shanghai
                    September 19. My plans are now to leave here on plane already scheduled to
                    depart Saturday, September 23.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hurley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
